{
 "about": "Mat Gallery v2 extra sections from Claude looking at the photos (Oct 20), after Tiffany said Red and Orange & Peach were too thin. Added on top of each mat's primary; Tiffany's calls in mat-color-overrides.json still set the primary. Holiday mats never get extra sections. 'florals' = multi-color floral designs: they show in Multicolor Florals in place of Multicolor (Aria, Calista, Tova keep their strong color too); 'florals_only' = floral mats with no single strong color, shown only in Multicolor Florals. v3 (Oct 20 late): 'also.earthy' = muted, low-saturation mats picked from the color data (tone muted) and checked by eye; 'also.animal' = leopard/cheetah/zebra/tiger/giraffe/cowhide/fawn prints, found by name + looking at every mat; 'also.pastel' = soft multi-color pastel mats (Multi-Pastel), checked by eye; 'primary_fix' = Claude's gallery-only primary corrections (Amahj Blue, Citron + Lilac was in Pink by mistake: pale blue-mint center, citron border, lilac field). v4: Brown & Tan merged into Earthy; 'tonal_fix' = Claude's re-check of every Neutral/Earthy/Dark/B&W mat against Tiffany's test (replaces those four tags only); 'holiday_off' = holiday-tagged mats with no Christmas/holiday motifs, moved to their color sections (year-round). v4: 'also.pastel' is now the broad Pastels section (any mat whose overall palette is pastel, single-color or multi; picked from the tone/lightness data and checked by eye). v4 Brights/Pastels pass: 'also.dark' = deep jewel-tone mats (navy, emerald, burgundy, black-ground florals) found while sorting the Brights bucket, so they sit in Dark & Moody instead of Brights.",
